# Input to the runtime lock. `make lock` compiles this into requirements.txt, which pins every
# third-party package the API needs at run time to an exact version and its hashes.
#
# The two local packages are listed so the resolver reads their dependencies from the working tree,
# and marked unsafe (see the Makefile) so they are left out of the output: a directory has no single
# file to hash, and carpool-domain is not on PyPI, so it must never be resolved from there. They are
# installed afterwards with --no-deps.
-e ./packages/domain
-e ./apps/api
